    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE Announcement</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/announce/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/announce/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;preamble&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Date: June 16, 2026&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The FreeBSD Release Engineering Team is pleased to announce the availability of FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE.&#xA;This is the second release of the stable/15 branch.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Some of the highlights:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;ulist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The iwlwifi(4) and other LinuxKPI based wireless networking drivers are now based on Linux v7.0.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;FreeBSD cloud images using packaged base systems now include pkg(8), and support automatic base system package updates on first boot.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A new kern.sched.name tunable allows the kernel scheduler to be selected at boot time.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Significant progress has been made towards complete support for the C23 version of the C programming language.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Unicode support has been updated to Unicode 17.0.0 and CLDR 48, adding 4,803 characters.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE EC2 AMIs</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/ec2-ami-ids/release/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/ec2-ami-ids/release/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_introduction&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This page lists EC2 AMIs for FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE.&#xA;You can filter the list of AMIs by region, architecture, flavour, and/or root filesystem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Note that these are the original images from the release and do not have any post-release security or errata fixes; you may want the &lt;a href=&#34;../latest&#34;&gt;latest patched AMIs for FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE&lt;/a&gt; instead.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These AMI IDs are available programmatically via the AWS SSM Parameter Store:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;literalblock&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;$ aws --region ${REGION} ssm get-parameter \&#xA;    --query &amp;#39;Parameter.Value&amp;#39; --output text \&#xA;    --name /aws/service/freebsd/${ARCH}/${FLAVOUR}/${FILESYSTEM}/15.1/RELEASE&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE EC2 Patched AMIs</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/ec2-ami-ids/latest/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/ec2-ami-ids/latest/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_introduction&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This page lists EC2 AMIs for FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE with the latest post-release security and errata fixes applied.&#xA;You can filter the list of AMIs by region, architecture, flavour, and/or root filesystem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A separate page lists the &lt;a href=&#34;../release&#34;&gt;original images from the release&lt;/a&gt; without any post-release security and errata fixes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These AMI IDs are available programmatically via the AWS SSM Parameter Store:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;literalblock&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;$ aws --region ${REGION} ssm get-parameter \&#xA;    --query &amp;#39;Parameter.Value&amp;#39; --output text \&#xA;    --name /aws/service/freebsd/${ARCH}/${FLAVOUR}/${FILESYSTEM}/15.1/RELEASE/latest&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE Errata</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/errata/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/errata/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This document lists errata items for FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, containing significant information discovered after the release or too late in the release cycle to be otherwise included in the release documentation.&#xA;This information includes security advisories, as well as news relating to the software or documentation that could affect its operation or usability.&#xA;An up-to-date version of this document should always be consulted before installing this version of FreeBSD.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This errata document for FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE will be maintained until the release of FreeBSD 15.2-RELEASE.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE README</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/readme/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/readme/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This document gives a brief introduction to FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE.&#xA;It includes some information on how to obtain FreeBSD, a listing of various ways to contact the FreeBSD Project, and pointers to some other sources of information.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_table_of_contents&#34;&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;ulist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#intro&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#obtain&#34;&gt;Obtaining FreeBSD&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#contacting&#34;&gt;Contacting the FreeBSD Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#seealso&#34;&gt;Further Reading&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#acknowledgements&#34;&gt;Acknowledgments&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;intro&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This distribution is a release of FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, the latest point along the 15-STABLE branch.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;about&#34;&gt;About FreeBSD&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;FreeBSD is an open source operating system derived from 4.4 BSD Lite2 for 64-bit x86-based PC hardware (amd64), 64-bit Arm® ARMv8-A AArch64 systems (aarch64), 32-bit Arm® ARMv7 systems (armv7), 64-bit PowerPC® systems (powerpc64, powerpc64le), and 64-bit RISC-V (riscv64) systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE Release Notes</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/relnotes/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/relnotes/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph abstract-title&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The release notes for FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE contain a summary of the changes made to the operating system on the 15-STABLE development line.&#xA;This document lists applicable security advisories and errata issued since the last release as well as significant changes to the ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;toc&#34; class=&#34;toc&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;toctitle&#34; class=&#34;title&#34;&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#intro&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#security-errata&#34;&gt;Security and Errata&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#security&#34;&gt;Security Advisories&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#errata&#34;&gt;Errata Notices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland&#34;&gt;Userland&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-packages&#34;&gt;System Packaging Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-config&#34;&gt;Userland Configuration Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-programs&#34;&gt;Userland Application Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-contrib&#34;&gt;Contributed Software&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-deprecated-programs&#34;&gt;Deprecated Applications&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-libraries&#34;&gt;Runtime Libraries and API&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#cloud&#34;&gt;Cloud Support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#kernel&#34;&gt;Kernel&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#kernel-general&#34;&gt;General Kernel Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#drivers&#34;&gt;Devices and Drivers&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#drivers-device&#34;&gt;Device Drivers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#drivers-removals&#34;&gt;Deprecated and Removed Drivers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage&#34;&gt;Storage&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage-general&#34;&gt;General Storage&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#_zfs&#34;&gt;ZFS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#_nfs&#34;&gt;NFS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#boot&#34;&gt;Boot Loader Changes&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#boot-loader&#34;&gt;Boot Loader Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#network&#34;&gt;Networking&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#network-general&#34;&gt;General Network&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#wireless-networking&#34;&gt;Wireless Networking&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#hardware&#34;&gt;Hardware Support&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#hardware-virtualization&#34;&gt;Virtualization Support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#documentation&#34;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#man-pages&#34;&gt;Man Pages&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE Upgrading Instructions</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/upgrading/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.1R/upgrading/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This note details the procedure for upgrading existing installations to FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;upgrade&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This document explains the procedure for upgrading existing 14.4-RELEASE or 15.0-RELEASE installations to 15.1-RELEASE.&#xA;Systems running older releases must be upgraded incrementally to one of these releases before performing this upgrade.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Before upgrading the operating system, back up &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt; filesystems, read the &lt;a href=&#34;../errata&#34;&gt;late-breaking errata&lt;/a&gt; for known issues and workarounds, and the &lt;a href=&#34;../relnotes&#34;&gt;release note&lt;/a&gt; for major changes and incompatibilities.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
